H8500.definition:
or תּוּכִּי;
probably of foreign derivation; some imported creature, probably a peacock
KJV: peacock.

H8503.definition:
from H3615 (כָּלָה);
completion; by implication, an extremity
KJV: end, perfect(-ion).

H8504.definition:
probably for H7827 (שְׁחֶלֶת);
the cerulean mussel, i.e. the color (violet) obtained therefrom or stuff dyed therewith
KJV: blue.

H8505.definition:
a primitive root;
to balance, i.e. measure out (by weight or dimension); figuratively, arrange, equalize, through the idea of levelling (ment. estimate, test)
KJV: bear up, direct, be (un-)equal, mete, ponder, tell, weigh.

H8506.definition:
from H8505 (תָּכַן);
a fixed quantity
KJV: measure, tale.

H8507.definition:
the same as H8506 (תֹּכֶן);
Token, a place in Palestine
KJV: Tochen.

H8508.definition:
from H8506 (תֹּכֶן);
admeasurement, i.e. consummation
KJV: pattern, sum.

H8509.definition:
apparently from an unused root meaning to encompass;
a wrapper or robe
KJV: garment.

H8510.definition:
by contraction from H8524 (תָּלַל);
a mound
KJV: heap, [idiom] strength.

H8511.definition:
a primitive root;
to suspend; figuratively (through hesitation) to be uncertain; by implication (of mental dependence) to habituate
KJV: be bent, hang (in doubt).

H8512.definition:
from H8510 (תֵּל) and H24 (אָבִיב); mound of green growth;
Tel-Abib, a place in Chaldaea
KJV: Tel-abib.

H8513.definition:
from H3811 (לָאָה);
distress
KJV: travail, travel, trouble.

H8514.definition:
from H3851 (לַהַב);
desiccation
KJV: great drought.

H8515.definition:
or תְּלַשַּׂר; of foreign derivation;
Telassar, a region of Assyria
KJV: Telassar.

H8516.definition:
from H3847 (לָבַשׁ);
a garment
KJV: clothing.

H8517.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7950 (שֶׁלֶג);
snow
KJV: snow.

H8518.definition:
a primitive root;
to suspend (especially to gibbet)
KJV: hang (up).

H8519.definition:
or תּלֻנָּה; from H3885 (לוּן) in the sense of obstinacy;
a grumbling
KJV: murmuring.

H8520.definition:
probably from an unused root meaning to dissever; breach;
Telach, an Israelite
KJV: Telah.

H8521.definition:
from H8510 (תֵּל) and the feminine of H2798 (חֲרָשִׁים); mound of workmanship;
Tel-Charsha, a place in Babylonia
KJV: Tel-haresha, Tel-harsa.

H8522.definition:
probably from H8518 (תָּלָה);
a quiver (as slung)
KJV: quiver.

H8523.definition:
(Aramaic) or תַּלְתִּי; (Aramaic), ordinal from H8532 (תְּלָת);
third
KJV: third.

H8524.definition:
a primitive root;
to pile up, i.e. elevate
KJV: eminent. Compare H2048 (הָתַל).

H8525.definition:
from an unused root meaning to accumulate;
a bank or terrace
KJV: furrow, ridge.

H8526.definition:
from H8525 (תֶּלֶם); ridged;
Talmai, the name of a Canaanite and a Syrian
KJV: Talmai.

H8527.definition:
from H3925 (לָמַד);
a pupil
KJV: scholar.

H8528.definition:
from H8510 (תֵּל) and H4417 (מֶלַח); mound of salt;
Tel-Melach, a place in Babylonia
KJV: Tel-melah.

H8529.definition:
a denominative from H8438 (תּוֹלָע);
to crimson, i.e. dye that color
KJV: [idiom] scarlet.

H8530.definition:
feminine from an unused root meaning to tower;
something tall, i.e. (plural collective) slenderness
KJV: armoury.

H8531.definition:
(Aramaic) from H8532 (תְּלָת);
a tertiary rank
KJV: third.

H8532.definition:
(Aramaic) masculine תְּלָתָה; (Aramaic), or תְּלָתָא; (Aramaic), corresponding to H7969 (שָׁלוֹשׁ);
three or third
KJV: third, three.

H8533.definition:
(Aramaic) multiple of H8532 (תְּלָת);
ten times three
KJV: thirty.

H8534.definition:
by reduplication, from H8524 (תָּלַל) through the idea of vibration;
a trailing bough (as pendulous)
KJV: bushy.

H8535.definition:
from H8552 (תָּמַם);
complete; usually (morally) pious; specifically, gentle, dear
KJV: coupled together, perfect, plain, undefiled, upright.

H8536.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8033 (שָׁם);
there
KJV: [idiom] thence, there, [idiom] where.

H8537.definition:
from H8552 (תָּמַם);
completeness; figuratively, prosperity; usually (morally) innocence
KJV: full, integrity, perfect(-ion), simplicity, upright(-ly, -ness), at a venture. See H8550 (תֻּמִּים).

H8538.definition:
feminine of H8537 (תֹּם);
innocence
KJV: integrity.

H8539.definition:
a primitive root;
to be in consternation
KJV: be amazed, be astonished, marvel(-lously), wonder.

H8540.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H8539 (תָּמַהּ);
a miracle
KJV: wonder.

H8542.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Tammuz, a Phoenician deity
KJV: Tammuz.

H8544.definition:
or תְּמֻנָה; from H4327 (מִין);
something portioned (i.e. fashioned) out, as ashape, i.e. (indefinitely) phantom, or (specifically) embodiment, or (figuratively) manifestation (of favor)
KJV: image, likeness, similitude.

H8545.definition:
from H4171 (מוּר);
barter, compensation
KJV: (ex-) change(-ing), recompense, restitution.

H8546.definition:
from H4191 (מוּת);
execution (as a doom)
KJV: death, die.

H8547.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Temach, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Tamah, Thamah.

H8548.definition:
from an unused root meaning to stretch;
properly, continuance (as indefinite extension); but used only (attributively as adjective) constant (or adverbially, constantly); ellipt. the regular (daily) sacrifice
KJV: alway(-s), continual (employment, -ly), daily, (n-)ever(-more), perpetual.

H8549.definition:
from H8552 (תָּמַם);
entire (literally, figuratively or morally); also (as noun) integrity, truth
KJV: without blemish, complete, full, perfect, sincerely (-ity), sound, without spot, undefiled, upright(-ly), whole.

H8550.definition:
plural of H8537 (תֹּם);
perfections, i.e. (techn.) one of the epithets of the objects in the high-priest's breastplate as an emblem of complete Truth
KJV: Thummim.

H8551.definition:
a primitive root;
to sustain; by implication, to obtain, keep fast; figuratively, to help, follow close
KJV: (take, up-) hold (up), maintain, retain, stay (up).

H8552.definition:
a primitive root;
to complete, in a good or a bad sense, literal, or figurative, transitive or intransitive
KJV: accomplish, cease, be clean (pass-) ed, consume, have done, (come to an, have an, make an) end, fail, come to the full, be all gone, [idiom] be all here, be (make) perfect, be spent, sum, be (shew self) upright, be wasted, whole.

H8553.definition:
from H4487 (מָנָה); a portion assigned;
Timnah, the name of two places in Palestine
KJV: Timnah, Timnath, Thimnathah.

H8554.definition:
patrial from H8553 (תִּמְנָה);
a Timnite or inhabitant of Timnah
KJV: Timnite.

H8555.definition:
from H4513 (מָנַע); restraint;
Timna, the name of two Edomites
KJV: Timna, Timnah.

H8556.definition:
or תִּמְנַת סֶרַח; from H8553 (תִּמְנָה) and H2775 (חֶרֶס); portion of (the) sun;
Timnath-Cheres, a place in Palestine
KJV: Timnath-heres, Timnath-serah.

H8557.definition:
from H4529 (מָסָה);
liquefaction, i.e. disappearance
KJV: melt.

H8558.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be erect;
a palm tree
KJV: palm (tree).

H8559.definition:
the same as H8558 (תָּמָר);
Tamar, the name of three women and a place
KJV: Tamar.

H8560.definition:
from the same root as H8558 (תָּמָר);
a palm trunk
KJV: palm tree.

H8561.definition:
(plural or (feminine) תִּמֹּרָה; (singular and plural), from the same root as H8558 (תָּמָר);
(architectural) a palm-like pilaster (i.e. umbellate)
KJV: palm tree.

H8562.definition:
or תַּמְרֻק; or תַּמְרִיק; from H4838 (מָרַק);
properly, a scouring, i.e. soap or perfumery forthe bath; figuratively, a detergent
KJV: [idiom] cleanse, (thing for) purification(-fying).

H8563.definition:
from H4843 (מָרַר);
bitterness (plural as collective)
KJV: [idiom] most bitter(-ly).

H8564.definition:
from the same root as H8558 (תָּמָר);
an erection, i.e. pillar (probably for a guide-board)
KJV: high heap.

H8565.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to elongate;
a monster (as preternaturally formed), i.e. a sea-serpent (or other huge marine animal); also a jackal (or other hideous land animal)
KJV: dragon, whale. Compare H8577 (תַּנִּין).

H8566.definition:
a primitive root;
to present (a mercenary inducement), i.e. bargain with (a harlot)
KJV: hire.

H8567.definition:
a primitive root (identical with through the idea of attributing honor);
to ascribe (praise), i.e. celebrate, commemorate
KJV: lament, rehearse.

H8568.definition:
probably feminine of H8565 (תַּן);
a female jackal
KJV: dragon.

H8569.definition:
from H5106 (נוּא);
alienation; by implication, enmity
KJV: breach of promise, occasion.

H8570.definition:
from H5107 (נוּב);
produce
KJV: fruit, increase.

H8571.definition:
perhaps from the same as H594 (אֲנָךְ) through the idea of protraction;
a pinnacle, i.e. extremity
KJV: tip.

H8572.definition:
from H5123 (נוּם);
drowsiness, i.e. sleep
KJV: slumber(-ing).

H8573.definition:
from H5130 (נוּף);
a brandishing (in threat); by implication, tumult; specifically, the official undulation of sacrificial offerings
KJV: offering, shaking, wave (offering).

H8574.definition:
from H5216 (נִיר);
a fire-pot
KJV: furnace, oven.

H8575.definition:
or תַּנְחֻם; and (feminine) תַּנְחוּמָה; from H5162 (נָחַם);
compassion, solace
KJV: comfort, consolation.

H8576.definition:
for H8575 (תַּנְחוּם) (feminine);
Tanchumeth, an Israelite
KJV: Tanhumeth.

H8577.definition:
or תַּנִּים; (Ezekiel 29:3), intensive from the same as H8565 (תַּן);
a marine or land monster, i.e. sea-serpent or jackal
KJV: dragon, sea-monster, serpent, whale.

H8578.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8147 (שְׁנַיִם);
second
KJV: second.

H8579.definition:
(Aramaic) from H8578 (תִּנְיָן);
a second time
KJV: again.

H8580.definition:
from H5395 (נָשַׁם);
properly, a hard breather, i.e. the name of two unclean creatures, a lizard and abird (both perhaps from changing color through their irascibility), probably the tree-toad and the water-hen
KJV: mole, swan.

H8581.definition:
a primitive root;
to loathe, i.e. (morally) detest
KJV: (make to be) abhor(-red), (be, commit more, do) abominable(-y), [idiom] utterly.

H8582.definition:
a primitive root;
to vacillate, i.e. reel or stray (literally or figuratively); also causative of both
KJV: (cause to) go astray, deceive, dissemble, (cause to, make to) err, pant, seduce, (make to) stagger, (cause to) wander, be out of the way.

H8584.definition:
from H5749 (עוּד);
attestation, i.e. a precept, usage
KJV: testimony.

H8585.definition:
from H5927 (עָלָה);
a channel (into which water is raised for irrigation); also a bandage or plaster (as placed upon a wound)
KJV: conduit, cured, healing, little river, trench, watercourse.

H8586.definition:
from H5953 (עָלַל);
caprice (as a fit coming on), i.e. vexation; concretely a tyrant
KJV: babe, delusion.

H8587.definition:
from H5956 (עָלַם);
a secret
KJV: thing that is hid, secret.

H8588.definition:
or תַּעֲנֻג; and (feminine) תַּעֲנֻגָה; from H6026 (עָנַג);
luxury
KJV: delicate, delight, pleasant.

H8589.definition:
from H6031 (עָנָה);
affliction (of self), i.e. fasting
KJV: heaviness.

H8590.definition:
or תַּעְנָךְ; of uncertain derivation;
Taanak or Tanak, a place in Palestine
KJV: Taanach, Tanach.

H8591.definition:
a primitive root;
to cheat; by analogy, to maltreat
KJV: deceive, misuse.

H8592.definition:
from H6105 (עָצַם);
might (plural collective)
KJV: power.

H8593.definition:
from H6168 (עָרָה);
a knife or razor (as making bare); also a scabbard (as being bare, i.e. empty)
KJV: (pen-) knife, razor, scabbard, shave, sheath.

H8594.definition:
from H6148 (עָרַב);
suretyship, i.e. (concretely) a pledge
KJV: [phrase] hostage.

H8595.definition:
from H8591 (תָּעַע);
a fraud
KJV: error.

H8596.definition:
from H8608 (תָּפַף) contracted;
a tambourine
KJV: tabret, timbrel.

H8597.definition:
or תִּפְאֶרֶת; from H6286 (פָּאַר);
ornament (abstractly or concretely, literally or figuratively)
KJV: beauty(-iful), bravery, comely, fair, glory(-ious), honour, majesty.

H8598.definition:
from H5301 (נָפַח);
an apple (from its fragrance), i.e. the fruit or the tree (probably includ. others of the pome order, as the quince, the orange, etc.)
KJV: apple (tree). See also H1054 (בֵּית תַּפּוּחַ).

H8599.definition:
the same as H8598 (תַּפּוּחַ);
Tappuach, the name of two places in Palestine, also of an Israelite
KJV: Tappuah.
